    "title": "Onalaska man accused of multiple arsons found not competent, committed to state facility - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sam Shilts ,\n9 hours ago LA CROSSE, Wis. (WKBT) — A judge has found an Onalaska man accused of setting multiple fires in July not competent to stand trial and ordered him committed. David Sheldon, 37, appeared Wednesday for a competency hearing in La Crosse County court. Judge Mark Huesmann found Sheldon incompetent and committed him to the Department of Health Services. The court ordered a review in 90 days. Read full article\n2",
